      "sword_ef": "100",
      "sword_vu": "VU",
      "tactic_notes": "<table style=\"width: 100%; height: 613px;\" border=\"1\"><colgroup><col style=\"width: 20.0262%;\"><col style=\"width: 18.9791%;\"><col style=\"width: 30.3665%;\"><col style=\"width: 30.6283%;\"></colgroup>\n<thead>\n<tr style=\"height: 17px;\">\n<td style=\"height: 17px;\"><strong>Name</strong></td>\n<td style=\"height: 17px;\"><strong>Actions</strong></td>\n<td style=\"height: 17px;\"><strong>Notes</strong></td>\n<td style=\"height: 17px;\"><strong>Recommendation</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody align=\"left\">\n<tr style=\"height: 91px;\">\n<td style=\"height: 91px;\">Burn Mechanic</td>\n<td style=\"height: 91px;\">\n<ol>\n<li>Any Eberon's<strong> Basic Attacks</strong></li>\n<li>Yarrick's <strong>Whirlwind Spear</strong></li>\n</ol>\n</td>\n<td style=\"height: 91px;\">Any of Eberon's <strong>Basic Attacks</strong> will apply <strong>Burn</strong>. Follow up with Yarrick's <strong>Whirlwind Spear</strong> for guaranteed AOE damage.</td>\n<td style=\"height: 91px;\">\n<p>Eberon's 🏹 <strong>Darkfire Wings</strong> is especially good for spreading <strong>Burn.</strong></p>\n<p>Use Yarrick's <strong>Whirlwind Spear</strong> when there are multiple players with <strong>Burn</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 82px;\">\n<td style=\"height: 82px;\">Basic Attack Combo</td>\n<td style=\"height: 82px;\">\n<ol>\n<li>Eberon's ⚔️<strong>Darkfire Claw</strong></li>\n<li>Yarrick's ⚔️<strong>Ebon Spear</strong> (Free)</li>\n</ol>\n</td>\n<td style=\"height: 82px;\">Basic combo starting with Eberon's ⚔️<strong>Darkfire Claw</strong> which, on hit, chained into Yarrick's<strong> ⚔️Ebon Spear</strong>.</td>\n<td style=\"height: 82px;\">&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 122px;\">\n<td style=\"height: 122px;\">Advance Attack Combo</td>\n<td style=\"height: 122px;\">\n<ol>\n<li>Yarrick's ⚔️<strong>Deceptive Sweep</strong></li>\n<li>Eberon's ⚔️<strong>Darkfire Claw</strong> (Free)</li>\n<li>Yarrick's ⚔️<strong>Ebon Spear</strong> (Free)</li>\n</ol>\n</td>\n<td style=\"height: 122px;\">\n<p>Advance Attack Combo that players can choose to take a hit and be <strong>Slowed</strong>, <strong>or</strong> be followed-up with <strong>Basic Attack Combo</strong>.</p>\n<p>Since Deceptive Sweep has <strong>Multi(2)</strong>, it can start <strong>2 Basic Attack Combo</strong> on 2 different players.</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"height: 122px;\">Use during latter half on the fight (HP &lt; 50%)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 50px;\">\n<td style=\"height: 50px;\">Anti-Tank by Grapple</td>\n<td style=\"height: 50px;\">\n<ol>\n<li>Eberon's ⚔️ <strong>Darkfire Tail Stab</strong></li>\n</ol>\n</td>\n<td style=\"height: 50px;\">\n<p>Apply <strong>Grappled&nbsp;</strong>witth Eberon's ⚔️ <strong>Darkfire Tail Stab&nbsp;</strong>to minimize Tank player influence.</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"height: 50px;\">Use when Tanky player become too reliable.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 69px;\">\n<td style=\"height: 69px;\">Anti-Air &amp; Anti Tank Combo</td>\n<td style=\"height: 69px;\">\n<ol>\n<li>Yarrick's 🏹<strong>Harpoon Toss</strong></li>\n<li>Eberon's ⚔️ <strong>Darkfire Tail Stab&nbsp;</strong>(Free)</li>\n</ol>\n</td>\n<td style=\"height: 69px;\">\n<p>Start with Yarrick's 🏹<strong>Harpoon Toss</strong> that force <strong>Flying</strong> player to land and follow-up with Eberon's ⚔️ <strong>Darkfire Tail Stab</strong>.&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"height: 69px;\">Use when ST range attack is required.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 69px;\">\n<td style=\"height: 69px;\">AOE Nuke with guaranteed ST Damage</td>\n<td style=\"height: 69px;\">\n<ol>\n<li>Eberon's ⚔️ <strong>Darkfire Tail Stab</strong></li>\n<li><strong>⚔️ Stomp and Stab</strong></li>\n</ol>\n</td>\n<td style=\"height: 69px;\">\n<p>Attempt to apply <strong>Grappled</strong> with Eberon's ⚔️ <strong>Darkfire Tail Stab </strong>before launching <strong>⚔️ Stomp and Stab</strong> to deal massive AOE damage.</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"height: 69px;\">Use when majority of players are healthy, <strong>or </strong>when someone is <strong>Grappled</strong> and Yarrick and Eberon have spare turns.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 82px;\">\n<td style=\"height: 82px;\">Buff &amp; Debuff Passive</td>\n<td style=\"height: 82px;\">\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Hunger Debuff</strong> (Field)</li>\n<li><strong>Soulless Shell</strong> (Passive)</li>\n<li><strong>Cornered Monstrosity</strong> (Passive)</li>\n</ol>\n</td>\n<td style=\"height: 82px;\">\n<p>Take all Debuff from <strong>Hunger </strong>and other sources and convert them to extra Accuracy via <strong>Cornered Monstrosity. Soulless Shell&nbsp;</strong>prevents <strong>MIG </strong>and <strong>DEX </strong>dice from reducing.</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"height: 82px;\">&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style=\"height: 31px;\">\n<td style=\"height: 31px;\">Soulbroken Passive</td>\n<td style=\"height: 31px;\">\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Any Despair applying move</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Any the All-Defiled Attack</strong></li>\n</ol>\n</td>\n<td style=\"height: 31px;\">\n<p>Put players in Despair to apply SoulBroken faster.</p>\n</td>\n<td style=\"height: 31px;\">&nbsp;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Main Mechanic</strong></td>\n<td>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Empowering Stance; </strong>then, depends on Break Clock Status:\n<ol>\n<li><strong>&nbsp;</strong>Eberon's <strong>Prime Ebon Breath</strong></li>\n<li>&nbsp;Yarrick's <strong>SoulScream Strike</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Prime Ebon Veiled Strike</strong></li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n</ol>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p>Most powerful move locked behind its main mechanic of consuming all its turn and let the player make decision.</p>\n<p>Prime <strong>Ebon Breath</strong> is Single Target nuke while<strong> SoulScream Strike&nbsp;</strong>is strong AOE attack that scales with unfilled Yarrick's Break Clock sections.</p>\n<p><strong>Prime Ebon Veiled Strike&nbsp;</strong>is super powerful Single Target attack that scales with all unfilled Break Clock sections.</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p>Use on the first turn of a round when there are around 6-8 combined unfilled Break Clock.</p>\n<p>Try to force player to make a choice <strong>or push for party wide extra turns.</strong></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Zero Power</strong></td>\n<td>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Soul Devouring</strong> (Passive)</li>\n<li><strong>Soul Defiled Spear</strong></li>\n</ol>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p>Check for any creature in <strong>Crisis </strong>at the end of all the All-Defiled turns and fills Break Clock accordingly.</p>\n<p><strong>Soul Defiled Spear&nbsp;</strong>deails unblockable damage and increases Soulbroken stacks. It works as a slow time bomb in the conflict.</p>\n</td>\n<td>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
